{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/865279-unknown-armies-sell-me-or-scare-me","id":865279,"title":"Unknown Armies: Sell Me or Scare Me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-13T19:49:20-07:00","id":865279,"title":"Unknown Armies: Sell Me or Scare Me","content":"I've been hearing about a game called <b>Unknown Armies</b>, and it almost sounds like a parody of the World of Darkness. Is it any good? Any thoughts would be appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:59:08-07:00","id":865282,"title":"","content":"Unknown armies is to world of darkness as what Paranoia is to a technocracy game if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:01:32-07:00","id":865284,"title":"","content":"It's not a parody of the WoD, but its writers (Greg Stolze, Ryan Macklin, Filamena Young, and others) have worked on WoD projects before. The tagline is something like &quot;Broken people trying to make the world a better place&quot;, which is a bit of a different mission statement. Its magic system is based on following strange rituals (thaumaturgy), merging oneself with an archetype (avatars), or following an obsession (adepts). The cosmology is sort of like cMage with reality being ultimately consensual. The game is best known for its multiple sanity/shock meters. <br /> <br /> If you want a parody of the WoD written by many WoD writers, look up Katanas and Trenchcoats. Good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T21:32:42-07:00","id":865318,"title":"","content":"It's probably my favorite game of all time.<br /> <br /> Unknown Armies (as of the newest edition) describes itself as &quot;a game about broken people trying to fix the universe.&quot; <br /> <br /> This is a world where belief shapes reality, but actual magic takes obsession to the point of insanity and active detriment to the health of your social life. The core of your character sheet is five different 'Shock Gauges,' measuring how well adapted or hurt you are to things like Violence or Isolation; you can be a cool badass who can break necks with a stare, but it also makes you a dead-eyed freak that struggles to feel emotion. The writing style is witty and brilliant throughout (it gives you things like a mystic order of McDonalds employees or a cult dedicated to an amateur pornstar who ascended out of our reality) and makes horror-influenced urban fantasy feel fresh for the first time in decades.<br /> <br /> Or you could just read the new rulebook, available to backers of the current Kickstarter but shared here for your reading pleasure: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4nd8zitpn6bdqn5/AAAgUanu5BFaWwog3GsaguDda?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/sh/4nd8zitpn...3GsaguDda?dl=0</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-14-2016, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:57:56-07:00","id":865402,"title":"","content":"Unlike Kult, I can recommend this game. I'm biased because I happen to like Greg and Filamena. They're both very nice people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:22:54-07:00","id":866693,"title":"","content":"Some ideas may be interesting to be used in another games, and a good system for madness/sanity system, but I don't like very much the core line about the archetype and avatars... and the system of magic, too freak, for example a path of magic about to be always drunk. Maybe some faction or monster could be added to my homemade mash-up settin, but nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T14:08:51-07:00","id":867044,"title":"","content":"I ran multiple campaigns of UA! It's a fine game, with a very unusual setting premise. I'd say it has very little in common with World of Darkness because all of its important actors are human... sometimes <i>too</i> human.If I had to sum up the game in one sentence, I'd say &quot;Imagine if new-age mysticism, unsubstantiated conspiracy theories, and folk superstitions were actually real... some of the time.&quot;<br /> <br /> UA is set in the World of Our Desires. Superficially, it is <i>exactly </i>the real world, warts and all - but with the addition of the Occult Underground. The Occult Underground is a fringe community of weirdos, economic roadkill, crazed political extremists, substance abusers, new-age mystics, pagan wannabes, and the occasional homeless enlightened master. Some of these people have discovered actual supernatural power by tapping into their own bizarre obsessions, or finding patterns of behavior that resonate powerfully with the collective unconscious of humankind, or little tricks that appear to trigger some kind of 'glitch' in reality. They obsessively hunt down bits and pieces of occult lore - folk superstitions, rumors on the street, emulating stuff you saw in the movies or read in a book once - often unable to make sense of the signal for the noise.<br /> <br /> Most of them get nowhere. They don't learn enough to change anything, or burn out and quit the underground to live 'normal' lives, or die alone, rejected by society for their offbeat behavior. But a few learn enough to gather little groups of friends, clients, &quot;true believers&quot;, or cultists around themselves and keep the Underground going. Some will found or join secret societies with an agenda, trying to steer the Undergound towards something. And a very lucky/unlucky few will become something like gods - possibly not by choice.<br /> <br /> Generally, the power that Magick [sic] gives you isn't better than anything you might have as a normal person. Maybe when you're drunk, you've got a sort of telekinesis that's good for lobbing bricks and bottles at people. That's great! But it won't put you on the level as a sober man with a shotgun. An oft-repeated maxim of the Underground is &quot;there's no such thing as a free lunch.&quot; In other words, in order to create a paranormal effect, you have to sacrifice something. These sacrifices range from being mildly inconvenient to life-threatening, and it's up to you to decide if it's worth it. In most cases the more magical power a person has, the crazier they are, which is why secret wizards <i><u>don't </u></i>rule the world. You, an average person, probably don't listen to what crazy people tell you<i>, </i>assuming they even have enough awareness of reality through their psychoses.<br /> <br /> The game actually tracks your sanity across multiple criteria - Violence, Isolation, Unnatural, Self, and Helplessness. When something happens to stress your character out, they could get Failed or Hardened notches in one of these tracks. A failed notch means you've got a growing phobia of that stressor, and a hardened notch means you've become inured to it. Neither one of these is desirable. Having a track full of Failed notches means you have a panic attack whenever you're attacked, left alone too long, see a two-headed dog, etc. Hardened notches do act as a kind of armor against stress (e.g. having 3 hardened notches in Violence means you'll never panic if you're hit during a fight), but having a full track of Hardened notches means you've become a kind of sociopath - you are completely unaffected by your stressor, no matter how bad it is (e.g. a person with 10 hardened Violence notches could torture their own mother to death and feel nothing). Taken all together, it's a pretty good system for modelling how a character can grow stranger over time.<br /> <br /> UA functions on three levels - Street, Global, and Cosmic. At the Street level, you're playing a random schmuck who might have some idea about the existence of the Occult Underground or has stumbled into it by accident. Your main goal is to learn enough to survive and decide if you dare to go any deeper. At the Global level, you've learned enough about Magick and the Underground to really make a difference in the community, and it's up to you to decide how that power will be used. At the Cosmic level, you know how Magick interacts with the cosmos, and you can take a stab at using that to knowledge literally change the World of Our Desires.<br /> <br /> The World of Our Desires is called that for a reason. One of the game's biggest conceits is that ordinary people <i>do </i>have the power to make a difference, to change the world into the shape they think it should have. But what happens when people disagree on the world's shape? They struggle against each other, of course. These struggles define our reality in a very literal sense, because the ultimate cosmic powers who govern in the Living Mirror of Heaven are all people. The Archetypes, as they are known to the Underground, are sort of like elected representatives who govern the cosmos. Each was once a human, and each has an agenda in line with what some part of humanity wants for itself. Archetypes can be replaced or fall out of relevance as the average person's beliefs shift, but while they last they have the ability to manipulate probabilities, make subtle but broad adjustments to how human society works, and grant supernatural power to people who act in an archetypal manner.<br /> <br /> The dice mechanics run on a d% system in which most players will fail most rolls. This is by design, since UA is meant to be a horror game - the growing panic and uncertainty in the face of danger is reinforced by bad rolls, which makes the lucky rolls all the more cathartic. That said, if you're STing a game you need to be <i>really </i>careful about when you make players roll and what for, because nobody likes to screw up doing routine tasks in a stress-free situation or to feel like they're doomed because they can't do anything right in a crisis. Playing UA as more of an action game is possible, but you have to make sure the players have enough skill points to consistently succeed in their areas of focus.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd say it's an excellent game and I'd recommend it to anyone who likes tabletop RPGs, horror, post-modernism, and/or the crazy urban legends you read about on Snopes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T16:47:35-07:00","id":868888,"title":"","content":"I love Unknown Armies and if I ever had a chance I'd play/run the shit about it. It's amazingly well written and currently the 3rd edition is on kickstarter right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T01:05:43-07:00","id":869174,"title":"","content":"The system of magic is too boring to me, with freak obssesions. The &quot;archetypes&quot; from the invisible clergy are beings without true personality. The classic gods from Greek-Roman, Egyptian or Viking myths were beings with personal traits. <br /> <br /> What is the main plot? What about &quot;supernatural creatures&quot; like spirits? <br /> <br /> Maybe I would rather the WoD-clone Witchcraft by Eden Studios. <br /> <br /> This background couldn't be used for a videogame, maybe for a short fiction readen in only a evening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:22:03-07:00","id":872154,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the link, <b>atamajakki</b>. Actually getting to read some of the material was very helpful<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/865279-unknown-armies-sell-me-or-scare-me?p=865282#post865282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unknown armies is to world of darkness as what Paranoia is to a technocracy game if that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got to love a good six-pack of clones. All praise to the Computer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T00:26:05-07:00","id":872191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/865279-unknown-armies-sell-me-or-scare-me?p=869174#post869174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system of magic is too boring to me, with freak obssesions. The &quot;archetypes&quot; from the invisible clergy are beings without true personality. The classic gods from Greek-Roman, Egyptian or Viking myths were beings with personal traits. <br /> <br /> What is the main plot? What about &quot;supernatural creatures&quot; like spirits? <br /> <br /> Maybe I would rather the WoD-clone Witchcraft by Eden Studios. <br /> <br /> This background couldn't be used for a videogame, maybe for a short fiction readen in only a evening.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Archetypes are just that - archetypes. They aren't gods, they're the symbolic building blocks, the important masks and roles of the human race across the globe, and the whole point of them is that they can be overtaken by different people in the hopes of shaping a better world. You don't pray to The Naked Goddess, you attempt to become her so that what she represents can form the bedrock of the human shared consciousness.<br /> <br /> The main plot is the obsessions of broken people trying o change what the world is. It's about trying to force your crazy paradoxical worldview on the universe before some else does it and fucks everything up. The few factions and NPCs are just there for inspiration, really; in such a human-centric, belief-fueled setting, the story is whatever the fuck your player characters bring to the table. Do they want to reshape the nature of reality? Do they want to find and murder the guy that killed their brother? Do they want to find the Holy Grail in the middle of the American South? Do they want to become the incarnate gods of the internet, or sell salvation out of a Mexican-Korean fusion food truck?<br /> <br /> It's the game of postmodern magick. It's about breaking the rules and being broken by them. It's a setting where all your shiny superpowers have a cost paid in your ability to function as a normal person. It's the rare fictional universe where the cosmos isn't cruel and infinite and unyielding and Lovecraftian, but instead one shaped by the whims and failings of the human race. I'd take that over another run of the mill urban fantasy setting made of stale, recycled tropes any day, and certainly not something that you yourself describe as a clone of another franchise.<br /> <br /> You may think there's nothing there, but it's been enough to spawn a dozen books, a successful Kickstarter, and lots of really excited fans. I'm sorry you're missing out on all the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-23-2016, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:15:00-07:00","id":872268,"title":"","content":"But the antagonist aren't interesting for me, I would rather the marauders from Mage: the Ascesion or the archonts from Kult: lost divinity. <br /> <br /> I only like from UA the game system for madness/sanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:15:03-07:00","id":872937,"title":"","content":"I know Filamena (and have since before she moved out of the US) and she's great people. Heck, she once used a couple of base ideas I and someone else put down to make a cult that &quot;hunts&quot; Mummies to devour them. I don't remember the exact question, but it was something like &quot;What would you do with a being you could never kill, that would regenerate from everything.&quot; One person said they'd feast on it, and I said I'd make sure it stayed slumbering and dreaming for all eternity. She did a lot more with it, but good stuff. High quality and one of not just the greats in the industry, but a nice person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}